<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20036" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλᾱκ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be slack, lazy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.3.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.8.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Hom.</u>
				p.39
			</span></i> O., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῇ κατατάσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. καὶ ἀποδειλιᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					9.31
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			 (which is cited from <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i> by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1405.32
			</span></i>), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυφάω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.27
			</span></i>; but 
				Act.
			 in this sense, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Arc.</u>
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>lose</i> or <i>waste through laziness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Ep.Sat.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
